# Preferred script export style

When shipping distributable scripts (Scriptable, userscripts, bookmarklets, browser helpers, or similar):

1. **Prefer a single-file standalone export** over multi-file `importModule` / split modules for end users.
2. **Host on GitHub** (or another stable public URL) and publish **raw download links**.
3. Include **Tampermonkey-compatible metadata** at the top of the distributable file:
   - `@name`, `@namespace`, `@version`, `@description`, `@author`
   - `@downloadURL` and `@updateURL` pointing at the same raw/CDN URL
   - A safe `@match` (or early runtime guard) so the script does not break normal browsing if installed in Tampermonkey for updates only
4. Also publish a **`.user.js`** twin of the same file when useful for one-click Tampermonkey install/update.
5. Prefer **jsDelivr** (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/<owner>/<repo>@<ref>/path`) and/or **raw.githubusercontent.com** links in README.
6. Bump `@version` whenever the distributable changes so auto-updaters pick it up.
7. Keep modular source in-repo for development; regenerate standalones with the project bundler before release.

This is the user's preferred export/distribution style — use it by default for future script packaging unless they ask otherwise.
